WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.621
Record what was actually done and
observed, with the configuration,

2
00:00:04.741 --> 00:00:07.913
instruments, conditions and execution
details.

3
00:00:08.033 --> 00:00:11.446
A copied expected result is not an
observation.

4
00:00:11.566 --> 00:00:15.498
If a step was not executed, say so and
retain the reason.

5
00:00:15.617 --> 00:00:20.721
Distinguish a justified exclusion from a
test that could not be completed.

6
00:00:21.341 --> 00:00:25.893
Retain applicable original records, raw
electronic data, printouts

7
00:00:26.013 --> 00:00:29.944
and photographs under the defined
retention arrangements.

8
00:00:30.064 --> 00:00:32.409
Link summaries to those originals.

9
00:00:32.529 --> 00:00:35.356
The required period depends on the record

10
00:00:35.476 --> 00:00:40.255
and applicable obligations; this module
supplies no universal number.

11
00:00:40.375 --> 00:00:43.298
Preserve readability, access and integrity

12
00:00:43.418 --> 00:00:47.142
rather than keeping only a polished report
screenshot.

13
00:00:47.762 --> 00:00:49.900
If logging stops during a test,

14
00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:53.675
retain the partial record and document
what happened.

15
00:00:53.795 --> 00:00:56.623
Assess which conclusions the gap affects.

16
00:00:56.743 --> 00:01:01.225
Do not fill the missing interval from
memory or copy another run.

17
00:01:01.345 --> 00:01:05.505
Any continuation or repeat needs the
defined procedure,

18
00:01:05.625 --> 00:01:10.315
a documented rationale and a clear
relationship to the first record.

19
00:01:10.935 --> 00:01:13.969
Corrections must preserve the original
entry

20
00:01:14.089 --> 00:01:18.779
and identify the change according to the
applicable record controls.

21
00:01:18.899 --> 00:01:22.003
For paper, avoid obscuring the earlier
value.

22
00:01:22.123 --> 00:01:26.467
For electronic records, use the authorized
correction mechanism

23
00:01:26.587 --> 00:01:28.587
and applicable audit trail.

24
00:01:28.707 --> 00:01:32.501
A reviewer should be able to reconstruct
the chronology

25
00:01:32.621 --> 00:01:36.414
rather than encounter an unexplained clean
replacement.
